      {
        "id": 243200,
        "name": "",
        "username": "The_Justifier",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/the_justifier/{size}/4954_2.png",
        "created_at": "2022-03-06T18:15:16.281Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"fjur\" data-post=\"20\" data-topic=\"29147\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/fjur/48/4849_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> fjur:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I can definitely see the OblivAeon event happening in this reality, and Writhe would certainly fit right in as a Scion.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>By definition, OblivAeon happens in every reality that’s part of the Multiverse, and thus pretty much by definition, if the characters exist as anything other than fiction, they’ll face OA when the time comes.</p>\n<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"TakeWalker\" data-post=\"17\" data-topic=\"29147\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/takewalker/48/5677_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> TakeWalker:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Vertigo would be a great hero name</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>If you want a hero to use such a sinister sounding name, you should probably include an honorific.  I think Lady Vertigo has almost certainly been used somewhere, but Sir Vertigo sounds really good and is probably obscure enough to be original.</p>",
